use /lib

export shape TableMeasuringShape:
    description:
        The rows out of view are measured a few at a time over the frames
        after they arrive, so the scrollbar comes to know the table's full
        height without any one frame laying out every row. Until a row has been
        measured, it counts as tall as it last was, or as the rows measured so
        far on average.

    resizing:
        When the table's width changes, only the rows in view are laid out
        anew straight away, staying where they are, and the rest are measured
        again the same way.

    steadiness:
        Once measured, the scrollbar's thumb holds still: it never jumps as
        rows come into view while scrolling, and rows added below while
        scrolled away from the end leave it where it is.
